%9Setting:%9

    print_whois_rpl_in_active_window (boolean; default: ON)

%9Description:%9

    Prints WHOIS and WHOWAS replies in the active window.

    print_whois_rpl_in_server_window comes first: when it is ON and the
    network has a status window (named after the server tag), the replies
    go there. Otherwise this setting puts them in the window you are
    looking at.

    With both settings OFF the replies go to the usual window: a query
    with the nick, or the window that matches the message level.

%9Examples:%9

    /SET print_whois_rpl_in_active_window on
    /SET print_whois_rpl_in_active_window off

%9See also:%9

    SET, WHOIS, WHOWAS, PRINT_WHOIS_RPL_IN_SERVER_WINDOW
